---
source: crates/kipi-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
kipi: a scoped map of your local repos and shared skills for LLM coding agents.

Usage: kipi [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init         Create a store and mount it, or mount an existing one
  stores       List mounted stores, or unmount one
  scan         Find git repos under scope roots (or PATHs) and record them
  add          Add a skill, a repo entry or a scope
  remove       Remove a repo entry
  scope        Change a scope: its registry, roots, parent, skills or always-on files
  bind         Add skills, relations, exclusions or aliases to a repo entry
  unbind       Remove skills, relations, exclusions or aliases from a repo entry
  resolve      Print the resolved plan (no side effects)
  explain      Show where every decision for a repo comes from
  sync         Materialize the plan into repos (and their linked worktrees)
  status       Per-repo sync state and always-on tokens vs budget
  tree         Stores → scopes → repos → skills, with provenance markers
  where        Resolve an alias to a repo, its summary and paths
  grep         Search skills, notes and conventions (and checkouts with --repos)
  edit         Open a repo entry, skill, scope:<name>, notes:<repo> or conventions:<scope> in $EDITOR
  doctor       Check stores, repos and grants for problems
  hook         Install or remove the git hook that syncs each new worktree
  completions  Print shell completions
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --store <PATH>  Mount this store instead of the configured ones (repeatable; before the subcommand)
      --json          Print machine-readable JSON (see docs/json.md)
      --no-color      Never color output (NO_COLOR is respected too)
  -v, --verbose...    Say more on stderr (repeatable)
  -q, --quiet         Say nothing on stderr but errors
  -h, --help          Print help
  -V, --version       Print version
